# launchcontrol deployment env — copy to deploy/launchcontrol.env and edit.
# (deploy/launchcontrol.env is gitignored; never commit real secrets.)
#
# Branding, access gates, PAX standings, and season scoring policy are no
# longer env vars — they live on the League/Season/ScoringSystem rows in
# the database. First boot (`prisma migrate deploy`) seeds only the
# built-in `pca-rmr` league. To add your own club/league, run the CLIs
# inside the running web container, e.g. for a fresh RMsolo deployment:
#
#   docker compose exec web pnpm --filter web league:create \
#     --slug rmsolo --name "Rocky Mountain Solo" --gate optional
#   docker compose exec web pnpm --filter web season:create \
#     --league rmsolo --name "2026 Summer Series" --year 2026 --planned 10
#
# See README.md's "Leagues & Seasons" section for the full CLI reference
# (branding flags, scoring presets/policy files, etc).

# Which league legacy routes (/, /leaderboard, ...) serve. Must match a
# league slug that exists in the database (the seeded default is pca-rmr).
DEFAULT_LEAGUE_SLUG=pca-rmr

# --- Ingest sidecar (only used with `docker compose --profile ingest`) ---
# Which league the RMsolo poller ingests results into. Leave unset/empty
# to fall back to DEFAULT_LEAGUE_SLUG.
INGEST_LEAGUE=
# How often the ingest sidecar polls rmsolo.org (seconds). Default every 30 minutes.
INGEST_INTERVAL_SECONDS=1800

# --- On-demand "Ingest now" admin button ---
# compose.yaml already sets INGEST_NOW_ENABLED=1 on the web service (poppler is
# installed in the image, so the capability probe passes). It surfaces a
# capability-gated "Ingest now" button on each league's admin dashboard that
# runs the same RMsolo scrape on demand. Set to anything other than "1" (or
# remove it from compose.yaml) to hide the button — e.g. a deployment that only
# ingests via the sidecar or admin .axdb uploads and wants no manual trigger.
# INGEST_NOW_ENABLED=1

# SESSION_SECRET is REQUIRED for any league whose accessGate is "required"
# (the seeded pca-rmr default) — every page for that league checks a signed
# session cookie even before MSR credentials exist, and 500s without it.
# Leagues created with --gate optional/none don't need it. 32+ random chars,
# e.g.: openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Optional: MSR login (leave unset until org-scoped credentials exist) ---
# MSR_CONSUMER_KEY=
# MSR_CONSUMER_SECRET=
# MSR_ORG_ID=
# MSR_OAUTH_CALLBACK_URL=https://your-host/api/auth/msr/callback
# ADMIN_MSR_UIDS=
